I find the phone number for my local medical clinic.
The number is thirty-two, forty-five, sixty-seven, eighty-nine.
I call them and wait a few minutes.
A friendly receptionist answers the phone.
"Medical clinic, you are speaking with Hanna," she says.
I explain that I have become really sick today.
"My head is heavy, and my eyes itch," I say.
I also tell her that my throat hurts.
She asks if I have a fever.
I answer that I do not think so, but I am very tired.
"You ought to speak with a doctor today," the receptionist says.
She looks in the calendar to find an appointment.
"Can you come at one o'clock?" she asks.
"Yes, that fits perfectly," I reply.
"Remember to bring your yellow health card," she says.
I thank her and hang up.
Now I just need to relax a bit before I walk over there.
